{"target": "minidb/tokens.py, minidb/nodes.py", "findings": ["minidb/nodes.py: the helpers signal caller bugs with ValueError (children/walk/expr_source on a non-node, output_name on an aliasless Star item, i.e. every `SELECT *` item), so a planner/engine slip surfaces as ValueError rather than QueryError -> expand Star items before calling output_name, and wrap helper calls at the planner/engine boundary with `except ValueError as exc: raise QueryError(...) from exc` instead of relying on api.py's catch-all.", "minidb/nodes.py: expr_source renders the normalised operator and repr'd numbers, so an unaliased `a != b` is named \"a<>b\" and `1.50*2` is named \"1.5*2\", contradicting the Output naming rule (source text with whitespace removed) whenever SelectItem.source_text is empty -> the parser must always populate SelectItem.source_text from the raw SQL slice; treat expr_source only as a debug rendering, never as an output name.", "minidb/tokens.py: Token.value for `!=` is normalised to `<>` while Token.text keeps `!=`, so source text rebuilt from token values loses the original spelling -> build SelectItem.source_text by slicing the original sql between the first token's pos and the end of the last token (pos + len(text)), not by concatenating token values.", "minidb/nodes.py: AGGREGATE_FUNCTIONS/SCALAR_FUNCTIONS duplicate the key sets of functions.AGGREGATES/functions.SCALARS, so the two can drift and a name present only in nodes' frozenset would hit the engine as a KeyError on my dicts -> classify and validate function names with `name.upper() in SCALARS` / `in AGGREGATES` from functions.py (nodes' sets advisory only), and never index either dict without that membership test.", "minidb/nodes.py: FuncCall.name preserves the source spelling (`sum`, `Count`), while my published dicts are keyed by upper-case name only -> always look up SCALARS[name.upper()] / AGGREGATES[name.upper()]; is_aggregate_call already upper-cases, so the engine must do the same rather than passing FuncCall.name through.", "minidb/nodes.py: COUNT(*) is FuncCall(\"COUNT\", (), True) and carries no argument expression -> for star=True the engine must call AGGREGATES[\"COUNT\"] with one non-None placeholder per group row (e.g. [1] * len(group_rows)); an empty sequence would report 0 for every group, and a sequence containing Nones would undercount.", "minidb/tokens.py: any word matching a keyword case-insensitively becomes a KEYWORD token, so a column or table legitimately named `order`, `in`, `as` or `count` can never be referenced even though identifiers are case-sensitive per spec -> where the grammar unambiguously expects an identifier, accept a KEYWORD token and use Token.text (the original case) as the identifier.", "minidb/tokens.py: _scan_number accepts exponent forms (`1e5`, `2E-3`) that the specified literal grammar does not include, so such text becomes a valid float instead of a QueryError -> either restrict _scan_number to digits with an optional fractional part, or accept the extension deliberately; nothing downstream should assume NUMBER tokens have integer/decimal source text."]}
